# PicWise's front door on its own server (owner, 2026-10-30: «Θέλω να βλέπω live το
# site από το καινούργιο server»): HTTPS for picwise.subby.cloud in front of the site,
# which gunicorn serves on 127.0.0.1:8016 only (deployment/server/picwise-web.service).
# Put in place by deployment/web/web_setup.sh once the domain points at the server;
# Caddy then takes the certificate from Let's Encrypt by itself, renews it by itself,
# and sends http:// to https://. It passes the visitor's Host on and tells the site the
# request came over HTTPS, so the site's own links are https://picwise.subby.cloud ones.
{
	# HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 only: HTTP/3 would need UDP 443, which the firewall keeps
	# closed (deployment/server/base_setup.sh), and browsers would try it first.
	servers {
		protocols h1 h2
	}
}

picwise.subby.cloud {
	encode zstd gzip
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=63072000"
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8016
}
